T*
(National Cadet Corps \(NCC\) — Official Directorate General Training Notes) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. PRINCIPLES OF CAMOUFLAGE: Camouflage is the artificial disguise applied) Tj
T*
(to personnel, weapons, and equipment to blend seamlessly with surrounding) Tj
T*
(natural terrain.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. TYPES OF COVER: Cover from View \(conceals from enemy observation but) Tj
T*
(does not stop high-velocity bullets, e.g. tall grass, bush\); Cover from) Tj
T*
(Fire \(protects against enemy bullet penetration and artillery splinters,) Tj
T*
(e.g. thick rock walls, sandbagged trenches, earthen embankments\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. PERSONAL CAMOUFLAGE TECHNIQUES: 1. Helmet garnishing with local) Tj
T*
(vegetation matched to terrain; 2. Face and skin disruption using camouflage) Tj
T*
(cream or mud to break facial shine and natural highlights \(nose,) Tj
T*
(cheekbones\); 3. Wrapping rifle furniture in burlap/scrim to break the dark) Tj
T*
(weapon silhouette.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. DISCIPLINE OF CONCEALMENT: Avoid sudden movements, do not look over the) Tj
T*
(top of a parapet when you can observe around its side, and avoid breaking) Tj
T*
(the skyline.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
